    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31077" root="عول" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُعْوَلٌ</span></b> , followed by <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَلَيْهِ</span>, <i>Wailed for:</i> thus in
the trad., <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المُعْوَلُ عَلَيْهِ يُعَذَّبُ</span>, (S, O,) or, as some
relate it, ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المُعَوَّلُ</span></b> ; i. e. <i>He</i> (of the dead) <i>who is
wailed for will be punished.</i> (O.)

